00:31:38.730 --> 00:31:44.230
Now, the next thing that I'm
going to demonstrate is--

00:31:44.230 --> 00:31:46.290
so I know that my queue
can dispatch tasks

00:31:46.290 --> 00:31:48.180
at a certain rate,
but how do I determine

00:31:48.180 --> 00:31:51.810
what is the optimal rate
of this entire system?

00:31:51.810 --> 00:31:55.570
And I'm going to run a small
sensory analysis using my queue

00:31:55.570 --> 00:31:57.870
with the end microservice.

00:31:57.870 --> 00:32:00.720
And what I've done
is I've forcefully

00:32:00.720 --> 00:32:05.100
disabled auto scaling at the
end cluster, the GKE cluster,

