00:35:43.040 --> 00:35:44.450
So apologize for that delay.

00:35:47.380 --> 00:35:48.140
Yeah, there we go.

00:35:48.140 --> 00:35:51.040
So we got the rate set.

00:35:51.040 --> 00:35:53.360
And we see that the
higher rate is set here.

00:35:53.360 --> 00:35:56.350
So as this higher rate is set,
what you need to understand

00:35:56.350 --> 00:35:57.160
is--

00:35:57.160 --> 00:35:59.650
OK, I was doing one per
second, now I've done 10 times.

00:35:59.650 --> 00:36:04.120
And this 10 points per second,
this rate is also is good,

00:36:04.120 --> 00:36:08.350
but I want to understand,
is this good enough?

00:36:08.350 --> 00:36:12.070
And we can see that
at the output queue.

00:36:12.070 --> 00:36:14.620
We also see the outputs
getting processed.

00:36:14.620 --> 00:36:17.660
But the Cloud Tasks queue
I feel could do better.

00:36:17.660 --> 00:36:20.050
And one of the things about
this particular feature

00:36:20.050 --> 00:36:23.330
is that it helps you do
a sensitivity analysis.

00:36:23.330 --> 00:36:26.560
So we have 10 tasks per second,
and we can go all the way up

